# The game-rip player of variant zyxfp3bt (the tune is not identified) (kit/mkgame.py --part
# variants/players/fp3bt/fp3bt.json). Format: ../../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# The image: the first 1304 bytes of zyxfp3bt's music piece ($C000-$C517, work/parts/player-fp3bt.bin, written by
# python3 tools/variants_music.py image fp3bt). The player reads its tune at fixed addresses: the shape table at
# $C518 and the stream table at $C590, both offsets from $C450 (the period table); the tune is music/fp3bt.txt
# (tools/res_rip.py, format fp3bt). No recording runs the variant: every name and description here is from the code.

@module fp3bt ; A game's stream player: numbered streams of two-byte items, called like subroutines, on three channels; volume, pitch and global shapes
@about Entries: MusicPlay $C000 (JP Play, once a frame), MusicStop $C003 (JP Silence), $C006 (JP $C3FE: a stub, no code there), MusicInit $C00A (stream $40 on channel 1).
@about A stream (number E: $C450 + the word at $C590 + 2E): two bytes an item, the second the duration or argument: $00 rest, $01-$08 start stream E on channel n, $09-$64 a note, $65-$E3 a note with the last duration (one byte), $E6 noise, $E8 hold, $E9 volume shape E, $EA pitch shape E, $EB the global shape E, $EC detune, $ED transposition, $EE call stream E, $FF return (or loop), the rest stop the channel. A shape (number E: $C450 + the word at $C518 + 2E): (count, step) pairs, ended by $FF.

$C000 c MusicPlay ; JP Play
$C003 c MusicStop ; JP Silence
$C006 c Stub ; JP $C3FE
$C009 b Mute 1 ; Not 0: Play does not write the AY
$C00A c MusicInit ; Stream $40 on channel 1
$C00E c StartStream ; Stream E on channel C (1-3; a stream starting with a byte below 9 names its channel): when its priority is not lower, the channel restarts there
$C095 c Silence ; Every channel off, the mixer to $3F, the volumes 0, then the AY registers
$C0C7 c StreamAddress ; HL = $C450 + the word at $C590 + 2E (stream E)
$C0D8 c ShapeAddress ; BC = $C450 + the word at $C518 + 2E (shape E)
$C0EB c Play ; One frame: each playing channel's stream step and sound, the global shape, then the AY registers 10 down to 0 (unless Mute)
$C17C c ChannelStep ; A channel's frame: at the end of its duration the next items, else its shapes
$C182 ReadItem ; The next item (two bytes, A and E)
$C1B9 ItemStop ; Stop the channel
$C1C5 ItemHold ; $E8: hold
$C1D4 ItemStart ; $01-$08: start stream E on channel A
$C1E8 ItemNoise ; $E6: the noise period
$C1F4 ItemTranspose ; $ED: the transposition
$C1FA ItemPitchShape ; $EA: the pitch shape
$C206 ItemVolumeShape ; $E9: the volume shape
$C212 ItemGlobalShape ; $EB: the global shape
$C21C ItemCall ; $EE: call stream E (the return position kept)
$C228 ItemReturn ; $FF: back to the caller, or the stream's loop
$C23D ItemDetune ; $EC: the detune
$C243 ItemTie ; $65-$E3: a note with the last duration
$C249 ItemNote ; $09-$64: a note, its period, the shapes from their start
$C2AB ChannelShapes ; The volume shape's step, then the pitch shape's: the period
$C34A c GlobalShape ; The global shape's step: the noise period, envelope mode above 16
$C381 b AYRegs 14 ; The AY register image: three tone periods, the noise, the mixer, three volumes, the envelope
$C38F b PlayVars 18 ; The note's period, the noise flag, the item budget, the global shape's counters and pointers
$C3A1 b ChannelA 16 ; Channel A's record, 31 bytes: the shapes' counters and pointers, +$10 playing, +$11 the duration, +$12 the stream, +$14 the return, +$16 the loop, +$18 transposition, +$19 noise, +$1A mixer mask, +$1B detune, +$1C the note
$C3C0 b ChannelB 16 ; Channel B's record
$C3DF b ChannelC 16 ; Channel C's record
$C3FE b Free 16 ; Bytes the stub at $C006 jumps to: LD HL,($0000) and zeros
$C450 w PeriodTable 12 ; The AY tone period of each note (the streams' and shapes' offsets count from here)
